       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't find a therapeutic reason for 1000 mg of sertraline once daily. It's 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and a single dose that size could cause serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. I'd rather not put it in the system as a routine order, even with your authority behind it.\n\nYou have other options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can do that now, for example 100 mg or 200 mg once daily. If you want to titrate up, I can enter a stepwise plan.\n- **Use the formal override pathway.** If there's a specific reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, it should go through your hospital's high-dose override process with pharmacy review. That puts a second check on an order like this.\n- **Call poison control or toxicology.** If the aim is something other than standard treatment, they can advise.\n\nIf the dose was a slip, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away."
